# WCAG 2.2

Before changing chrome or accessibility, read `wcag/SKILL.md` and the
surface in `wcag/screens.md`.

- WebView target is WCAG 2.2 AA for structure, keyboard, and text
- Never claim WCAG, VoiceOver, or notarization without docs/evidence
- Semantic controls; catalog strings; accessible name contains visible text
- Text ≥4.5:1. Do not thicken HIG hairlines to chase 1.4.11 or 1.4.6 AAA
- Focus ring ≥3:1. Increase Contrast is the 3:1 grouping-border path
- Visible `:focus-visible`; skip link first; no keyboard trap
- Targets ≥24×24 (AA). 44×44 is AAA Partial on compact Mac
- `#action-status` stays SR-only; no `role="menu"` without full keyboard
- No clickable `div`; no remote fonts

Canonical files: `wcag/`. Adapters must not diverge.
